---
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import "../styles/global.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <title>Privacy Direction | HarborNavi</title>
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="HarborNavi privacy direction for the harbornavi.com early access list."
    />
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon.svg" type="image/svg+xml" />
    <link rel="canonical" href="https://harbornavi.com/privacy" />
  </head>
  <body data-route="privacy">
    <SiteHeader activeRoute="privacy" />
    <main>
      <section class="privacy-page section-shell">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy direction</p>
        <h1>HarborNavi is being designed for local-first home intelligence.</h1>
        <p>
          This page explains the current public data flows for the product waitlist and 15 Homes Across America.
          It will be updated before either flow asks for materially different information.
        </p>
        <div class="privacy-grid">
          <article>
            <h2>Useful events first</h2>
            <p>
              HarborNavi is intended to help households choose useful events, review alerts, and save selected
              moments without turning every camera frame into another notification.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>No default cloud video promise</h2>
            <p>
              The product direction is local-first. HarborNavi should not require default cloud upload of raw home
              video, broad identification, or emergency response behavior.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Product email list</h2>
            <p>
              The <code>/home-v5</code> form collects an email address for HarborNavi Kickstarter and 15 Homes road updates.
              A configured email provider may store that address and its two topic subscriptions after the primary
              waitlist record is saved. You can unsubscribe anytime.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>15 Homes application</h2>
            <p>
              The host application is an external form. It may ask for contact details, metro area, availability, a
              high-level device or home-system summary, and readiness for a visit. Do not submit raw footage, camera
              credentials, or a full street address during initial screening.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Application consent</h2>
            <p>
              Applying allows the form provider and HarborNavi to process the answers and contact the applicant for
              screening. It is not a selection notice or a final filming release. Applicants must be 18 or authorized
              to apply; children are off camera by default.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Application launch gate</h2>
            <p>
              The external application stays disabled until HarborNavi publishes the provider name, retention window,
              deletion-request contact, and applicant rights. A form URL alone is not enough to open the application.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>Campaign analytics</h2>
            <p>
              First-party campaign analytics records page and link events with route, session, and attribution data.
              Application answers, email addresses, postal details, camera models, and household details are not sent
              as analytics event properties.
            </p>
          </article>
          <article>
            <h2>External video links</h2>
            <p>
              YouTube live and replay links open on YouTube. HarborNavi does not embed an autoplaying player on the
              15 Homes pages, so YouTube is not loaded simply by visiting those pages.
            </p>
          </article>
        </div>
        <p>
          To withdraw from campaign email, use the opt-out in a campaign message. Once the application gate is cleared,
          this page or the active form will identify the deletion-request contact and how applicants can exercise their
          published rights.
        </p>
      </section>
    </main>
    <footer class="site-footer">
      <span>HarborNavi</span>
      <a href="/home">Home</a>
    </footer>
  </body>
</html>
